<p>Five Italian nationals died during a scuba diving trip in the Maldives after failing to return from a deep cave dive in Vaavu Atoll, south of Malé, Italy’s Foreign Ministry said. Maldivian authorities recovered one body and were searching for four others believed to be inside the same underwater cave system, which officials said descends to about 60 meters. The University of Genoa said four of the victims were linked to the university: marine biology professor Monica Montefalcone, her daughter Giorgia Sommacal, researcher Muriel Oddenino and marine biology graduate Federico Gualtieri. Other reports identified the fifth victim as diving instructor and boat operations manager Gianluca Benedetti. The Italian Foreign Ministry said 20 other Italians aboard the Duke of York, the vessel involved in the expedition, were safe. Maldivian officials said rough seas and the cave’s depth made the recovery effort dangerous. A rescue dive on Friday ended without finding the four missing bodies, and authorities said searches would resume when conditions improved.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/pT3VWuZF6z49I9f4vqC2hpERoKX8feizS9zeaAsmKGH5mRebKXWXprnbXNKLEQLR0mguW97gi_RDxwJviiuPyVsnqDVwBb_79NyLX7RL-gMJXpb1DjLPfiy-xwBWrFu5uQTgS9eHD5sZ-U74yjqVgUHKz7xrCTZjLmOJYjAeH6m9CgzjnO7LWkkUPD7zWg' alt='Divers and guides returning to shore in Malé, capital of the Maldives, a popular diving destination.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Recovery assets: Tourism Minister Mohamed Ameen said coastguard officers and security forces were scouring remote seas around the cave, and officials sent a large Coast Guard vessel to support the operation.</li><li>Depth rules: Shareef said tourists were not supposed to dive below 30 meters and that a separate investigation would examine how the group went deeper.</li><li>Cave layout: Italian Ambassador Damiano Francovigh said the cave divides into three connected sections, with access through narrow passages complicating the search.</li><li>Local assessment: Local officials described the incident as the worst single diving accident recorded in the Maldives.</li></ul><blockquote>We are deeply saddened by this tragedy, and our thoughts and prayers are with the families of the deceased Italian, the missing four Italians and everyone affected - Maldives President Mohamed Muizzu</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Maldives government: President Mohamed Muizzu said the search for the remaining four Italians “remains our highest priority,” while a government spokesman said weather had made the recovery effort unsafe. (<a href='https://www.channelstv.com/2026/05/15/maldives-rescuers-search-for-four-drowned-italian-divers/'>Channels Television</a>)</li><li>Italian Foreign Ministry: Foreign Minister Antonio Tajani called the incident a disaster for Italy and said the government would do everything possible to recover the bodies; the ministry also sent additional personnel to Malé to support families and operations. (<a href='https://www.iltempo.it/attualita/2026/05/15/news/maldive-sub-giallo-allerta-meteo-verita-videocamera-gopro-subacquea-47746417/'>Il Tempo</a>)</li><li>University of Genoa: The university identified four victims linked to its marine biology and research community and expressed condolences after the deaths. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c62e0p7rd2ro'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>Italian prosecutors: Italian judicial authorities opened an investigation into the deaths while experienced divers joined recovery operations in the Maldives. (<a href='https://www.kathimerini.gr/world/564228823/italia-eisaggeliki-ereyna-gia-ton-thanato-ton-pente-italon-dyton-stis-maldives/'>Kathimerini</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/authorities-search-waters-in-the-maldives-after-five-italians-killed-in-a-cave-dive-accident/article70982534.ece'>Authorities search waters in the Maldives after five Italians killed in a cave dive accident</a> - thehindu.com</l